<title>HUNGARY: TRACTEBEL BOOSTS STAKE IN DUNAMENTI TO 50.31 PCT.</title>
<headline>TRACTEBEL BOOSTS STAKE IN DUNAMENTI TO 50.31 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian utility holding Tractebel SA boosted its stake in Hungary's Dunamenti power station to 50.31 percent from 48.76 percent by purchasing almost all of the shares of Dunamenti's employees, the Hungarian MTI news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Tractebel bought the employee shares for 612 million forints, or at 118 percent of the face value, the same rate at which it purchased the 48.76 percent stake from the state privatisation agency APV in December 1995, MTI said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
